# Intent suppression for wikihow.intent (OVOS-INTENT-2 §4.3): an utterance
# about the weather belongs to a dedicated skill and must never trigger a
# WikiHow lookup, even when it also names "wikihow". Referenced inline via
# <weather> so the weather vocabulary stays the single source of truth.
<weather>
# Live-probed false positive (MiniCroft, en-US): "search wikipedia for tie
# a tie" was claimed by wikihow.intent -- the fuzzy padatious matcher was
# treating "wikipedia" as a near-match for the "wiki how|wikihow" tokens in
# "search (wiki how|wikihow) (for|) {query}". Wikipedia lookups belong to
# ovos-skill-wikipedia, never to WikiHow, so any mention of "wikipedia" must
# veto this intent outright.
wikipedia
# Live-probed false positive (MiniCroft, en-US): "search wiktionary for tie
# a tie" was also claimed for the same reason -- "wiktionary" fuzzy-matches
# "wiki how|wikihow" just as readily. Dictionary lookups belong to a
# dictionary/wiktionary skill, never to WikiHow.
wiktionary
